<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav August trade gap $98 mln.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav August trade gap $98 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	  AUG	 JULY		   AUG 1995</p>
<p> Exports million USD   155	 154.2		     N.A.</p>
<p> Imports		   253	 257.6		     N.A.</p>
<p> Balance		 -  98     - 103.4		     N.A.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JANUARY TO AUG)</p>
<p> Exports million USD 1,101	 936.5		     N.A.</p>
<p> Imports		 2,265     1,937.3		     N.A.</p>
<p> Balance	     - 1,164    -1,000.8		     N.A.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Yugoslav August exports fell by 4.6 percent against previous month, and imports dropped by 20 percent against July.</p>
<p>Data refer to new Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for the previous year are not available as the country was under the international trade embargo which was suspended November 1995.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom +381 11 222 4254</p>
</text>
